  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "If the circles $x^{2}+y^{2}+2 x+2 k y+6=0$ and $x^{2}+y^{2}+2 k y+k=0$ intersect orthogonally. then $k$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "2Lurb",
      "text": "2 or $-\\frac{3}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Yb5lS",
      "text": "-2 or $-\\frac{3}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "T5yuz",
      "text": "2 or $\\frac{3}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "QJAMp",
      "text": "-2 or $\\frac{3}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Two circles are orthogonally if and only if $\\quad 2\\left(g_{1} g_{2}+f_{1} f_{2}\\right)=c_{1}+c_{2}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad 2[(1 \\times 0+(k) k]=6+k$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad 2 k^{2}=6+k$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad 2 k^{2}-k-6=0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad 2 k^{2}-4 k+3 k-6=0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\quad 2 k(k-2)+3(k-2)=0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad(k-2)(2 k+3)=0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad k=2-\\frac{3}{2}$",
    "image": null
  },
